v386f5: [SESSION] Clean disconnect now actually closes the session (no more ghost after a
      graceful client Exit/Quit). server.py only. Builds on v385f5's _teardown_session.

      RE of vcncNet.dll (loaded into Ghidra) settled what the client does on a clean close
      (FUN_007e71b0): a three-step handshake ExitAppSpace -> Disconnect -> Close, each blocking
      on a server reply. vcncDisconnect (@0x1000b43c) sends reliable command 2 and treats a reply
      whose command field == 0x64 as success (else / on timeout it logs 'Can't disconnect
      server'). Our pl2[3]=0x64 IS that ack. On the wire the disconnect is a normal reliable
      packet (command 2 at pl[2:4]) that arrives via the compound path (handle_compound ->
      inner_cmd==2), so the server already parsed and answered it correctly.

      THE BUG: the inner_cmd==2 handler sent the 0x64 reply and returned WITHOUT tearing the
      session down. DEBUG capture run_20260801_002705 shows it exactly: client sends ExitAppSpace
      then Disconnect, server replies (seq=25 'disconnect reply', ACKed OK), client pings a few
      more seconds and vanishes (10054) - and the session is STILL live afterwards. Ghost.
      (Earlier confusion: 'disconnect reply'/cmd==2 showed 0 in older logs because those sessions
      were all ungraceful window-kills that never sent vcncDisconnect; and one client log showed
      VCNCMD_FATALLOSTCONNECTION *before* the disconnect - that was the pre-v385f5 ghost-lockout
      window, where the connection was already dead so vcncDisconnect never transmitted.)

      FIX: both disconnect handlers (compound inner_cmd==2, and the non-compound post-auth cmd==2
      fallback) now send the 0x64 ack and THEN call _teardown_session(why='(client
      vcncDisconnect)'). send_rel is synchronous, so the client gets its ack before the session is
      torn down; the teardown broadcasts the pilot delete and frees the ClientNumber/slot. Result:
      a graceful Exit/Quit closes the session immediately and cleanly - the reconnect-reap
      (v385f5) remains the backstop only for ungraceful CTDs that never send a disconnect.

      NOTE: this does NOT tear down on ExitAppSpace (inner_cmd==5) - leaving the app space can be
      a return-to-menu while staying connected; only the explicit Disconnect closes the session.

      TEST: DEBUG on, clean menu-quit; expect 'inner vcncDisconnect -> disconnect reply +
      teardown' then the session gone (no lingering 10054 ghost, active_sessions back to baseline).

      REVERT: drop the two _teardown_session(why='(client vcncDisconnect)') calls.

