v384f5: [HANGAR] Fix each side showing only ~1/3 of its planes (the '9 GB planes' report).
      PRE-EXISTING bug, NOT the war-date feature - the date filter (v383f5) was exonerated:
      the short hangar appeared IDENTICALLY in dated and undated arenas, so the date push was
      never the cause. server.py only; behind a flag.

      SYMPTOM: a side's hangar showed a stride-3 subset of its roster - GB served 27 flyable
      planes (DEBUG plane-teams confirmed byte0 US=22 GB=27 SU=19 GE=23 JP=19 in the 1945 arena)
      but the client displayed only 9 = 27/3, at pool positions 0,3,6,9,12,15... That 3x is the
      signature of the client's msg-58 pool decoder (FUN_004eff50) reading the 0x3a catalog echo
      as (Size-1)/3 THREE-byte records while the bytes were flat 1-byte ids.

      ROOT CAUSE: the client UPLOADS the catalog as flat 1-byte ids and expects the echo back as
      3-byte records [id][ushort]. Under PLANE_FILTER_VIA_CATALOG=True (v381 and earlier) the
      filtered re-echo emitted proper 3-byte records, so the pool was correct. When v382 flipped
      to byte0 gating (PLANE_FILTER_VIA_CATALOG=False) to cure the nation-bleed, that re-echo
      stopped running - 0x3a fell through to the DEFAULT echo, which bounces the upload back
      VERBATIM (1-byte). Client then read (28-1)/3 = 9. The regression was invisible because we
      only ever verified nation isolation via the 0x3a UPLOAD counts, never the hangar DISPLAY.

      FIX: new flag CATALOG_ALWAYS_3BYTE_ECHO (True) makes the 3-byte RE-ENCODING of the 0x3a
      echo unconditional. Per-side FILTERING still only runs under PLANE_FILTER_VIA_CATALOG
      (byte0 gates the side under False, so no bleed returns); the echo is simply always
      re-encoded 1-byte -> 3-byte. Verified in isolation: a 27-id GB catalog now yields Size=82
      -> client reads (82-1)/3 = 27 (was Size=28 -> 9). Reuses the exact proven True-path packet
      builder (build_ingame_pkt sets Size=n exactly, so no pad/garbage records).

      REVERT: CATALOG_ALWAYS_3BYTE_ECHO=False restores the old verbatim-echo behaviour.

      TEST on a THROWAWAY arena: enter, open the hangar, confirm the side now lists its FULL
      roster (GB ~27-28, not 9). Watch run_*.log for 'cmd=0 sub=0x3a -> re-encoded N (3-byte
      recs, ...)'. The 0x3a path has CTD history - if the arena page asserts, flip the flag off.

