v383f5: [WAR-DATE] Per-arena war-date plane filter + client date push. NEW FEATURE (engine +
      web panel), opt-in per arena. Touches server.py AND web_server.py. DB backed up.
      *** OPT-IN + DORMANT: nothing changes until an admin ticks a war date on an arena. ***

      WHAT IT DOES: an arena can be marked with a full war DATE (day/month/year) from the web
      Arena Management panel (Edit Settings -> War date). When set: (1) aircraft that had not
      entered service by that date are hidden from that arena's hangars (a 1943 arena hides
      1944+ planes); (2) the date is pushed into the arena's GAME_DEF so the CLIENT shows it too.
      Unticked = no restriction (all planes), which is every existing arena's behaviour.

      WHY OPT-IN: the probe (probe_arena_dates.py) confirmed all current arenas carry the stock
      22-Jun-1941 default, so a blanket filter would strip every 1942+ plane from the everyday
      arenas. The feature does nothing unless settings_json.war_enabled=1 for that arena.

      HOW (all on the v382-proven-safe byte0 path, NO new wire mechanism):
        * PLANE_SERVICE_YEAR: intro year per plane (121, keyed by name, vetted with the pilots).
        * plane_camp_for_room / _session_slot_camp remap out-of-window planes to camp 7 (NU),
          which apply_plane_teams already writes as byte0 0x80 - hidden from all standard sides,
          NEVER 0x00, so no GameDef 1902 CTD. Zero new masking code.
        * apply_war_date / _gamedef_date_offset push the Reality date bytes (day/month/year u16 LE)
          into the decompressed GAME_DEF - length-preserving, same pipeline as the AA patch. Date
          offset VERIFIED against 5 live arenas (all read 22/06/1941 = raw 16 06 95 07).
        * web_server.py: 'War date (plane era)' section in the arena settings editor (checkbox +
          day/month/year), stored in settings_json; a date_read bridge shows the arena's current
          GAME_DEF date as the default. Server passes extract_date_from_gamedef as that bridge.

      FLAGS / REVERT: WAR_DATE_ENABLED=False kills the whole feature (filter + push) in one flag;
      WAR_DATE_PUSH_TO_CLIENT=False keeps the plane filter but stops rewriting the client's date.

      TEST FIRST on a THROWAWAY arena (methodology): tick a date (e.g. 01/01/1943), enter, and
      check (1) only <=1943 planes appear per side; (2) NO GameDef.cpp:1902 CTD; (3) the client's
      in-game date reads 1943; (4) side-switching doesn't hang HQ. Watch run_*.log for the
      'war-date @+... pushed to client' line. If anything asserts, untick the arena (or flip
      WAR_DATE_ENABLED=False) - existing arenas are untouched either way.

      NOTE (verification gap at deploy time): server.py was compile-verified byte-for-byte against
      the tested replica. web_server.py edits were clean single-region inserts and the inserted
      blocks parse in isolation + the server<->web bridge arg count matches (10/10), but the full
      web_server.py was not compiled in the sandbox. The game server imports web_server at startup,
      so a syntax error would surface immediately as an ImportError in the startup log - confirm a
      clean 'Web interface running' line after restart.

