v382f5: [HANGAR] PLANE_FILTER_VIA_CATALOG False again - now SAFE, grounded on a full FA.exe RE of
      the GAME_DEF codec. Fixes the per-side plane 'bleed' via the byte-0 flyability gate, and lays
      the foundation for mixed-team/coalition arenas. DEPLOYED after v380f5's CTD; DB backed up.
      *** TEST ON ONE THROWAWAY ARENA BEFORE BROAD USE - see falsify criteria. ***

      THE RE (four functions read in FA.exe, base 0x400000, saved to re_findings.md):
        - FUN_00438330  = flyability gate: flyable = *(gamedef+0x558+planeId*0x1c) & (1<<camp).
                          Pure 32-bit bitmask AND. Record is 0x1c (28) bytes in memory.
        - FUN_00575be0  = GameDef_Serialize: writes the wire blob. Per plane: byte0=mask; if mask==0
                          STOP (1-byte record); else emit marker(0xff no-hascamp) + 2 limit bytes.
        - FUN_0057bee0  = wire DESERIALIZER = THE crashing function (GameDef.cpp:1902 'Len==0').
                          Its plane loop keys ONLY on (mask==0?) and (marker==0xff?) and copies the
                          mask value VERBATIM into the flyability dword - it never validates it:
                              mask==0             -> 1-byte record   <-- the ONLY dangerous value
                              mask!=0 & [1]==0xff  -> 4-byte [mask][0xff][lim][lim]
                              mask!=0 & [1]!=0xff  -> 6-byte hascamp form
        - FUN_0057f610  = .cfg text parser: PlanesAvailable does mask|=(1<<camp); PlanesProhibited
                          does mask&=~(1<<camp). Confirms byte0 == per-camp bitmask.

      WHAT THIS SETTLES: the v380 (and v332) CTD was NOT 'bit 7 illegal' and NOT 'per-camp masks are
      unsafe'. It was ONLY that the v380 guard wrote byte0=0x00 for the NU planes. 0x00 flips the
      reader to its 1-byte branch while the server's fixed 4-byte writer emits 4 bytes -> the block
      desyncs -> leftover Len!=0 -> the 1902 assertion. Every NONZERO mask (0x01..0x10 per nation,
      0x80 for NU, or a coalition mask like 0x03/0x1c) parses IDENTICALLY to the stock 0x1f. Proven
      from the crashing function itself, not inferred from the writer.

      THE FIX (apply_plane_teams, False path): byte0 = (1<<camp) for camps 0..4
      (US=0x01 GB=0x02 SU=0x04 GE=0x08 JP=0x10); byte0 = 0x80 for camps 5..7 (NU) - a non-standard
      camp bit, so FUN_00438330 hides those planes from all five WWII sides while keeping the record
      the 4-byte form (mask nonzero). NEVER 0x00. Verified across all 121 slots: correct per-nation
      masks, the four NU planes (Me-163B/Ouragan/Tunnan/HA-200) all 0x80, and ZERO planes at 0x00.
      The other 0x00 writer, apply_plane_hide, stays OFF (STAFF_HIDE_VIA_GAMEDEF=False), so no 0x00
      reaches the arena-page block from any path. apply_plane_byte0_override still sets Me-163B=0x80
      (now a no-op vs the teams pass) and continues to hard-refuse 0x00.

      MIXED TEAMS (future): the gate is a bitmask, so a coalition arena is a one-line change here -
      OR the member camps' bits instead of a single bit: US+GB -> 0x03, GE+JP+SU -> 0x1c. No new
      mechanism; FUN_00438330 already coalition-filters correctly. Noted at the code site.

      FALSIFY (throwaway arena first): (1) each side's hangar shows ONLY its own nation's planes
      (bleed gone); (2) NO GameDef.cpp:1902 CTD on the arena page; (3) side-switching does not hang
      the HQ menu. If (2) or (3) fail, flip PLANE_FILTER_VIA_CATALOG back to True (one flag) -> the
      bleed returns but the arena page is stable. KNOWN OPEN: whether 0x80 actually surfaces the NU
      planes ON the NU tab (vs merely hiding them from standard sides) is not yet observed - check
      an admin's NU hangar in the same test.

