v381f5: [HANGAR - REVERT of v380f5] PLANE_FILTER_VIA_CATALOG back to True. v380f5 (False) CTD'd
      EVERY client at the arena page: GameDef.cpp:1902 'Assertion failed (Len==0)' (messages89.log),
      the same assertion as the historical v332 CTD. Server restored to the known-good runtime
      behaviour (== v379f5).

      CORRECTED ROOT CAUSE: the crash was NOT the standard per-nation 1<<camp masks (US=0x01 ...
      JP=0x10). It was the camp>=5 guard I added in v380, which wrote byte0 = 0x00 for the four NU
      planes (Me-163B, Ouragan, Tunnan, HA-200). 0x00 = no camp bit set is EXACTLY the value the
      GAME_DEF parser rejects - it is the documented v332 trigger, and apply_plane_byte0_override
      already hard-REFUSES 0x00 for this precise reason. My guard wrote 0x00 directly in
      apply_plane_teams, bypassing that refusal, and it landed in the arena-page GAME_DEF served to
      everyone -> universal CTD. I had the v380 hazard exactly backwards: I wrote 0x00 to AVOID the
      (untested) bit-7 0x80, but 0x00 is itself the crash.

      THE DEEPER, DURABLE CONCLUSION: the GAME_DEF byte-0 flyability gate CANNOT express 'hidden from
      all standard sides' safely. Every nonzero byte-0 value files the plane on SOME nation tab;
      0x00 crashes the parser; bits 5/6/7 are untested. apply_plane_hide does write 0x00 but only on
      non-arena-page paths that never reach the shared arena GAME_DEF. This is the actual reason
      PLANE_FILTER_VIA_CATALOG=True has to exist: the 0x3a echo removes NU/staff planes from the LIST
      so their byte0 can stay the safe 0x1f. => The byte-0 gate is a DEAD END for the per-side
      'bleed' as long as any NU/staff-only plane is in the pool. Do NOT set False again; it CTDs
      every client.

      NET STATE: the hangar 'bleed' (all nations' planes visible on every side) is a KNOWN COSMETIC
      ISSUE, reverted to the stable pre-v380 behaviour. A real fix would have to drive the nation-tab
      display by some mechanism OTHER than GAME_DEF byte0, OR remove all NU/staff-only planes from
      the pool so byte0 masking becomes safe - neither attempted here. The v380 camp>=5 guard line
      remains in apply_plane_teams as DEAD CODE (only reachable on the False path, which is now off);
      left in place so the hazard is documented at the site, but it must be changed from 0x00 before
      False is ever revisited.

