v380f5: [HANGAR] PLANE_FILTER_VIA_CATALOG = True -> False. Switches per-side hangar filtering from
      the 0x3a catalog echo (which never actually filtered the DISPLAY) to the native GAME_DEF
      byte-0 flyability gate. Addresses the 'other nations' planes bleed into every side' symptom.

      WHY (settled after the v375-v379 detour): the client draws each plane's nation TAB from the
      GAME_DEF plane-info array byte 0 (FUN_006de570; documented in the apply_plane_byte0_override
      docstring), NOT from the 0x3a echo. Under True, apply_plane_teams writes byte0=0x1f (all camps)
      for every plane, so the GAME_DEF says 'every plane belongs to every side' and the hangar shows
      the full all-nation list on every side - exactly the bleed. The 0x3a echo only ever controlled
      list MEMBERSHIP, never the nation-tab display, so it could not fix the bleed no matter what it
      sent. This was NOT an ordering bug: Me-163B is correctly hidden for a non-mod, which proves the
      byte0-override at slot 118 hit the right plane => the GAME_DEF plane block is in PLANE_ROSTER
      order, and all three orderings (PLANE_ROSTER, the 0x3a upload id-space, the GAME_DEF block)
      agree. (This is also why v378's Preload-order reorder was wrong and was reverted in v379.)

      FIX: False makes apply_plane_teams write byte0 = (1<<camp) per plane, so FUN_00438330 greys
      wrong-nation planes and each side's hangar shows only its own aircraft. Verified per slot:
      US=0x01 GB=0x02 SU=0x04 GE=0x08 JP=0x10, correctly assigned to Pe-8->SU, A6M2->JPN,
      Dauntless->GB, C-47A/SBD-2->USA, etc.

      SAFETY (the v332 bit-7 CTD): under False, camp 7 (NU) would make apply_plane_teams write
