v374f5: [ECONOMY] JULY 2004 TC SCORING MODEL implemented from the 2004_07 official Fighter Ace
      newsletter ("Scoring Changes - What they are and what they mean"). This REPLACES the older
      ~2001 scoring.htm model (v249) with the 2004 TC rebalance. Master flag TC_ECONOMY_2004 (True);
      set False for the exact v249 model back. All values below validated against the newsletter's
      own worked examples on the deployed file.

      WHAT CHANGED (the 2004 model is different IN KIND from v249):
        * KILL = a FLAT Destroy Plane Bonus (500 pts), NOT the victim's plane value and NOT a rank
          ratio. In v249 a kill paid plane_value + (target_rank/killer_rank)x100; that whole
          mechanic is gone in 2004.
        * LOSS = the victim's plane BASE value scaled by the victim's RANK, via the rank/scoring
          modifier table (Cdt 5% ... Gen/FM 100%), plus a flat pilot loss penalty if the pilot
          actually died. A bail over friendly ground survives -> plane cost only. Crash-land in
          friendly territory is half (already handled). The newsletter's worked example reproduces
          exactly: base-2000 F4U-4C -> Cdt pays 100, LtCol 1000, Gen 2000.
        * The rank/scoring table ABANDONED all level differences in 2004 - the only rank effect now
          is the flat percentage above.

      CONSTANTS (all VERBATIM from the newsletter's final adjusted list):
        RANK_LOSS_MODIFIER_2004 = Cdt 5, Sgt 10, 2Lt 15, 1Lt 20, Cpt 30, Maj 40, LtCol 50, Col 60,
          BGen 70, MGen 80, LtGen 90, Gen 100, FM 100 (%).
        PILOT_LOSS_PENALTY_2004 = 500 *** FLAGGED VALUE ***: the newsletter self-contradicts - the
          prose says the pilot loss penalty was raised 250->1000, but the final "complete list ...
          after these adjustments" shows 500. Defaulted to 500 (the final list) per the maintainer;
          change the one constant to 1000 for the headline value.
        DESTROY_PLANE_BONUS_2004=500, DAMAGE_PLANE_BONUS_2004=250, DESTROY_HUMAN_PARACHUTE_PEN=500,
          DESTROY_AI_PARATROOPER_BONUS=50, TRIGGER_SCENE_BONUS_2004=1000, CAPTURE_SCENE_BONUS_2004=
          2000. (Kill/loss are wired now; the parachute/paratrooper/scene bonuses are defined and
          ready for when those events are attributed - nothing consumes them yet, like the existing
          GROUND_TARGET_VALUES.)
        TANK_VALUES_2004 = GE Tiger 500, SU KV-1 500, SU T-34 400, GE Panther 400, GB Cromwell 250,
          US Sherman 250, JP Type 97 100 (verbatim; defined for when ground scoring lands).

      PLANE VALUES (PLANE_VALUE_2004): *** PARTLY DERIVED - READ THIS ***. The newsletter gives only
      FOUR explicit 2004 values (Ki-100 800, Seafire III 600, Spit F Vb Trop 400, Hurricane IID 400)
      and a qualitative range (fighters 1000..2000, F4U-4C/Tempest near 2000, dedicated bombers
      lower). The full 121-plane table lived on Information/scoring.htm, which we DO NOT HAVE. So:
      the 4 explicit values are set EXACTLY; F4U-4C and Tempest are pinned to 2000 (the newsletter
      names them as the top of the band); the remaining ~115 are DERIVED by rescaling the v249
      relative ordering into the stated bands (fighters 1000..2000, bombers 600..1200). These are a
      faithful interpolation, NOT authoritative 2004 numbers. IF THE REAL scoring.htm TABLE SURFACES,
      replace the PLANE_VALUE_2004 dict wholesale - the mechanics around it are already correct.

      NOT WIRED YET (defined, waiting on their subsystems): the damage-plane bonus (needs per-hit
      damage attribution from msg 28 - see the ASSIST work), the parachute/paratrooper bonuses
      (need parachuter-hit detection), the scene trigger/capture bonuses and tank/ground values
      (need ground scoring), and the newsletter's Team Balance modifier (score x enemy/your team
      ratio - needs live per-team head-counts; noted for a later pass).

      REVERT: TC_ECONOMY_2004=False restores the v249 model exactly (kill_score + old plane table +
      flat 100/100). FALSIFY: fly a fresh session and read the SCORE log - a kill shows
      "+500 = Destroy Plane Bonus"; a death shows "-N = plane BASE x RANK% + 500 pilot loss"; a
      low-rank pilot pays a tiny fraction of a high-rank pilot for the same airframe; a bail shows
      plane cost only, no pilot-loss penalty.

