v372f5: [SCORE/CTD] Two fixes from the v371f5 field run (run_20260729_210316 + messages06/07).
      The 9-bit seq fix HELD - three clients crossed 255 with downlinks staying LIVE (SEQ9
      'crossed 255' for Bigalon/Taurus/Moira, continued 'in' deliveries after; no menus/
      invisibility/wedge). These two are the remaining fallout.

  (1) PARACHUTER-PRIME CTD - a v371f5 regression, now fixed. ALL41_MAD crashed at
      'There is no GamerClientScore for Client=1' (VNet.cpp:474, messages07 21:32), immediately
      after 'Create NetParachuter ONumber=303' for Taurus's (Client=1) bail. ROOT CAUSE: the
      parachuter-create (msg-2) binds the canopy to the bailing pilot's score object, and the
      msg-25 'parachuter prime' we send just before it is what CREATES that score object on the
      peer. v371f5 moved ALL msg-25 to the unreliable channel - but THIS one is not idempotent,
      it is an ORDERING PREREQUISITE: if the prime is dropped or arrives after the create, the
      create references a score object that does not exist -> CTD. This is exactly the
      ordering-dependency risk flagged when 25 went unreliable. FIX: send_stat_block_25 gains a
      force_reliable arg; the parachuter prime passes force_reliable=True so it goes reliable
      (guaranteed to arrive, and before the reliable create which takes a higher seq). The general
      scoreboard refresh stays unreliable (genuinely idempotent). Revert: force_reliable is opt-in;
      or set SEND_STAT25_UNREL=False to put all 25s back on reliable.
      FALSIFY: repeated bails by multiple pilots, no 'GamerClientScore for Client=N' CTD on any
      peer; the prime 25 logs as reliable (TX/RELIABLE) not unreliable for the parachuter path.

  (2) MISSING CYAN KILL BANNER on non-bail kills - GENERALISED the v368/v369 announce. The banner
      only fired for kills where the relayed delete carried the HUNTER id (the long shot-down exit
      form). Damage-latched deaths, plane explosions, and husk-downs all relay the SHORT 3-byte
      SYNTHESISED exit-tail (no hunter), so the shooter's client had nothing to announce even
      though we scored the kill server-side. messages06: MEC=1/1, MEC=4/4 and MEC=5/0 husk-downs
      all scored but showed NO 'destroyed' banner; the husk-down even labelled the dead target by
      AIRCRAFT TYPE ('Spit-IXe(0)') because no pilot object was bound on the peer. The bail case
      (v368/v369) was just the first instance of this whole class. FIX (ANNOUNCE_SYNTH_KILL): when
      a kill is scored (_killer known) but the relayed tail was synthesised (_hunter is None), send
