RE-VERIFICATION (vcncnet.dll, Ghidra) - v364f5 UNWRAP CONFIRMED AGAINST THE ENCODER.
      No code change. Loaded vcncnet.dll (the module that actually builds the wrapper -
      it is a separate binary from FA.exe, which only holds import thunks) and read the
      encoder directly. Findings:
      * vcncSendMessage @0x1000baf5 and vcncAddMessageToList @0x1000be4c are the send
        path. Each sub-message is emitted as [uCmd:2 BE][innerlen:2 BE][body], and the
        whole sub-message is padded UP to a 4-byte multiple (uVar6=(len+3)&~3).
      * The wrapper we strip is the outer sub-message header; uCmd's low byte is the
        FA message Type T, whose HIGH NIBBLE is the size (Size=T>>4) - the same
        bc*16+Size relation in the baseline notes, confirmed from the binary.
      * THIS IS WHY v364f5's predicate is correct, not lucky: 8+pl[4]*16+(pl[5]>>4)==len
        reduces, for a wrapped inner with bc=0, to 8+(T>>4)==len = [4B outer hdr]+
        [4B inner hdr]+[T>>4 body]. That is the client's genuine framing invariant,
        not a fitted heuristic. Re-checked: matches 25/25 distinct field samples.
      * FA.exe dispatcher @0x004f18a0 confirmed: indexes (&DAT_00c81ed8)[msg[0]] and
        calls handler(msg,len); unknown types are logged, not fatal. Validates the
        dispatch-table formula and the type-byte model the whole server relies on.

      TWO THEORETICAL EDGES the encoder revealed (NOT fixed - no observed frame hits
      them, and a speculative pad-aware rewrite REGRESSED 13/25 real samples in test,
      so the exact-equality predicate stays):
        (a) 4-byte PADDING: a sub-message whose body is not already 4-aligned would
            arrive with 1-3 pad bytes, and the exact-length check would REJECT it
            (false negative -> that message swallowed, as pre-v364). Every field
            sample was already aligned, so this is unobserved.
        (b) MULTI-SUB-MESSAGE LISTS: vcncAddMessageToList concatenates several subs
            under one send; the unwrap strips only the first 4B layer. A true 2-message
            list would fail the equality and fall through un-stripped.
      FALSIFICATION / when to revisit: if the field logs ever show a 'counter-wrap'
      REFRAME MISS on a frame whose (len-8) is not a multiple of 4, edge (a) is real -
      switch the check to `padded == len` AND simultaneously handle the direct-frame
      collision that broke the naive attempt (the regression came from dropping the
      exact-equality direct guard). If a swallowed message's payload decodes as two
      stacked [00 T 00 00] headers, edge (b) is real - loop the strip. Until a real
      frame exhibits either, leave v364f5 untouched.

