v360f5: [WIRE/CTD] *** PARACHUTE CTD - the compound echo path leaked ExitEvent(-1). ***
      Bailing out could crash the BAILER's client ~35s later, at the moment the
      parachuter touched the ground. Roulette odds: only when the client happened to
      wrap that one report in the 0x0542 prefix. Latent in v356 and every build since
      the prefixed/compound path existed; NOT an f5 regression.

      THE CRASH (messages63.log, session run_20260728_120928):
        09:15:33  out 33'15 ExitEvent(256) ScoreEvent=3        <- bail intent, valid Number
        09:15:34  out 4'15                                     <- parachuter create
        09:16:09.650  'Player crashed into ground' -> out 33'8 ExitEvent(-1):
                      the parachuter object is already deleted, so the report
                      carries Number = 0xFFFF
        09:16:09.671  in 33'8   <- the server ECHOED it back, 21ms round trip
        CTD: 'bounds error class ARR<class NET::OBJECT *,2048>[65535] 0..2047,
              ring.hpp line 27' - the inbound msg-33 handler (0x004f9ae0) indexes
              the NET::OBJECT ring by Number, and 65535 is out of bounds.

      WHY THE EXISTING GUARDS DIDN'T FIRE (server side, 12:16:09.651):
        The report arrived PREFIXED: REFRAME cmd=0x0542, pl=00040542|00820000|21 01ffff...
        All three defences for msg 33 - NO_ECHO_SUBS (v218), NO_ECHO_TYPES (v222) and
        the EXIT33 relay's 'never echo back to the sender' - live inside the cmd==0
        branch of handle_post_auth. cmd=0x0542 skips that branch entirely and falls
        through to handle_compound, whose OWN no-echo tuple was a stale pre-v222 copy:
        (0x20,0x03,0x45,0x18,0x53,0x54,0x4d,0x19) - no 0x21, no 0x0e. inner_sub=0x21
        fell to 'unknown inner -> echo inner' and the poison went straight back.
        Same guard-copy-divergence class as v342 (a fix applied to one wrapper path
        but not its twin).

      FIX (two edits, one vector - Number=0xFFFF must never reach ANY client):
      (1) handle_compound's no-echo tuple synced with the direct NO_ECHO_SUBS:
          0x21 (msg 33, this CTD) and 0x0e (msg 14 reassign, v204 rationale) added.
      (2) The direct-path EXIT33 peer relay now drops any ExitEvent whose
          id/AddData/Number region (stored[4:9]) contains adjacent ff ff - the -1
          form would otherwise be relayed VERBATIM to the peers and crash THEM
          (same handler, same ring index). Window deliberately stops at index 8:
          the real valid bail sample (12:15:33, Number=0x0100) carries ff ff ff ff
          from byte 9 on.
      Verified against real wire bytes: the fatal prefixed frame routes to swallow;
      the valid direct bail is NOT blocked by the relay filter; synthetic -1 forms
      with Number at 5:7 and 6:8 are both blocked. Compile-checked.

      FALSIFICATION: bail-outs (both sides watching) must land the parachuter with
      NO in 33 echo on the bailer and NO CTD; server log must show
      'inner sub=0x21 (notify, must not echo) - swallow' at the ground-crash moment.
      If a legitimate kill-credit event ever stops printing on peers after this
      version, check the EXIT33 'poison' log line first - a false positive there
      means a valid record carried ff ff inside bytes 4:9, and the filter needs a
      proper per-form Number decode instead of the pattern check.

      NOTE the same forensics exposed for the open bail-attribution issue (a): the
      DIRECT sub=0x21 form (e.g. the 12:15:33 bail intent, type=0xf2 sub=0x21) is
      swallowed by NO_ECHO_SUBS *before* the EXIT33 relay ever sees it - the relay
      only fires on the type-byte shape (tb==0x21, sub==0x00). So bail reports that
      arrive sub-form are never relayed and their hit records (the game's own
      kill-attribution payload) are discarded. That is likely a big piece of why
      bail kills score as 'solo crash'. Queued, not touched in this version.

