v359f5: [WIRE/CRITICAL] *** SERVER->CLIENT RELIABLE RETRANSMISSION - the 1.5-week bug. ***
      One lost downlink reliable datagram wedged the client's ENTIRE reliable RX channel
      permanently. Every symptom hunted since ~mid-July is this one mechanism:
      one-way invisibility, dead score panels, and the EMPTY HQ PLANE MENU.

      MECHANISM, from both ends:
        * The client's reliable RX is STRICTLY IN-ORDER (vcnc: 'QRcv :: Received
          expected packet N -> Now expecting packet N+1'; out-of-order arrivals are
          queued in nQSize, delivered only once the gap fills).
        * send_rel transmitted each seq EXACTLY ONCE and waited `to` for the ACK -
          no retransmission, ever. A dropped datagram left a PERMANENT hole at seq N.
        * The client then discarded/queued every later seq forever, while its own
          TX direction kept working - producing the signature ASYMMETRY.

      EVIDENCE (run_20260728_113009 + messages84 + messages62/vcnc on the Bigalon box):
        11:52:13/17/53  create Test2 0x0107 -> Bigalon sent THREE times (the relay's
                        re-create guard refiring) - never took: Bigalon flew blind to
                        Test2 from here on ('Test2 could see me, not the other way').
        11:53:09.452    STALL-WATCH: Bigalon reliable RX idle 21.8s, unreliable active,
                        pending_tx=1 - the downlink hole, seen from the server side.
        11:53:10.698    respawn create 0x0100 -> Bigalon: sent once into the wedged
                        channel, discarded like everything else.
        11:55:08        Bigalon exits to HQ -> client requests the msg-58 plane catalog
                        -> response discarded -> EMPTY PLANE SELECTION MENU. Test2 did
                        the identical HQ flow at 11:54:44 on a healthy channel and got
                        out 58'120 -> in 58'76 normally - msg 58 IS the hangar menu.
        11:55:44-11:57+ the client re-requests the ArenaList EVERY SECOND; the server
                        serves 208 responses; the client discards all of them. The
                        clearest possible picture of 'uplink alive, downlink wedged'.
      PREDATES the f5 line entirely - v356 and every build before it had the same
      single-shot send_rel; any session that lost one downlink datagram degraded this
      way. Two machines on a real network made the loss likely enough to see daily.

      FIX, two coupled changes (they MUST ship together):
      (1) send_rel now RETRANSMITS the SAME seq every REL_RETX_INTERVAL_S (0.75s)
          until ACKed or `to` expires. A late copy fills the client's QRcv hole and
          the queued backlog drains - full recovery instead of a permanent wedge.
          Healthy-path cost is ZERO: LAN ACKs arrive in ~10-15ms, far inside the
          first retransmit interval. Logged as 'RETX#n' + 'ACKed OK after n retx'.
      (2) LATE/DUP-ACK GUARD: rme() now records completed seqs in a 64-entry ring;
          an 8-byte pt=0 packet whose seq is in the ring is a benign duplicate or
          late ACK (counted in _late_ack_count), NOT a disconnect. Without this,
          retransmission would be DANGEROUS: a client that ACKs every received copy
          would have its second ACK land after rme() and be classified as a client
          disconnect -> broadcast leave + session pop on a live player. Also fixes
          the pre-existing late-ACK false-disconnect (an ACK arriving just after the
          send_rel timeout killed the session the same way).
      Verified in isolation: lost-first-copy recovers on RETX#1; completed seq
      correctly classifies as benign; total loss times out after ~5 retx cleanly.

      FALSIFICATION: healthy sessions must show zero or near-zero RETX lines and
      unchanged TX/RELIABLE 'ACKed OK' latency. If RETX lines are FREQUENT on a calm
      LAN, the ACKs themselves are being lost or misrouted - investigate before
      trusting anything else. If a session ever tears down right after a burst of
      RETX lines, the ring guard is not catching a dup-ACK shape - dump _late_ack_count
      and the RELRX ring first.

      STILL OPEN, deliberately untouched this pass: (a) bail-out kill attribution -
      11:53:00 Test2's death after bailing scored 'solo crash/crashland', no hunter
      credit (user-confirmed: the kill was earned); (b) cs9 wrap robustness - the
      stall-watch fired at cs=241 with the 255->0 wrap approaching; the wrap toggle's
      out-of-order mis-latch window is unfixed; (c) STALE-TICK 11:53:04 froze Test2's
      conductor tick for 3.8s during respawn - the v277 guard did its job but the
      root freeze is uncharacterised. One fix per version.

