v353: [SESSION] a re-join after exiting to the HQ left the previous in-game presence standing.
      Pilot loses visual of every other aircraft and nobody can see him.

      SYMPTOM (reported): ALL41_MAD exited to the HQ to change aircraft, joined again, and lost
      visual of all other aircraft; the others could not see him either.

      ROOT CAUSE: teardown_ingame_presence() existed (v348) but was wired ONLY into the REAP
      path, and the msg-64 back-to-lobby path has had its own teardown since v182. An HQ exit
      and re-join goes through NEITHER.
        15:02:08.392 LEAVE  _AvA_Insane pressed back-to-lobby (msg 64)   <- a proper leave
        15:02:37.580 DELETE3 ALL41_MAD ONumber=0x0104 (death)
        ...           NO [LEAVE] AND NO [TEARDOWN] FOR ALL41_MAD AT ALL
        15:06:47.098 ROOM   ALL41_MAD -> room 53 ClientNumber=0 PlayerIndex=0 (assigned)
        15:06:47.159 PLAYER62 broadcast join of ALL41_MAD -> 1 peer(s)
      15 teardowns fired in that file and none were his. Peers still held the old ALL41_MAD
      REMOTE_PLAYER at PlayerIndex 0 with his stale objects, so the msg-62 add landed on an
      already-occupied index - the client's "Add existing REMOTE_PLAYER" no-op - and neither
      side rebuilt the binding.

      FIX: tear down at the SLOT-ASSIGNMENT site instead of on yet another exit path. Chasing
      individual exit routes has now missed this twice (v182 covered msg 64, v348 covered reap,
      this went through neither). Every route back into a room passes through assign-room-slot,
      so tearing down there catches them all by construction, including routes not yet seen.

      THE GUARD IS THE POINT: entered_game is set when a session ENTERS the arena and is cleared
      by every clean exit. Finding it still True at slot-assignment time IS the stale-presence
      signal - a first join has it False and nothing fires. If [TEARDOWN] ever appears on a
      FIRST join, that guard assumption is wrong and this must be revisited immediately, because
      a spurious teardown produces the very invisibility it is meant to fix.

      DEADLOCK TRAP AVOIDED: the call MUST sit before the `with sl:` block.
      teardown_ingame_presence -> broadcast_object_delete_3 -> get_sessions_in_room takes `sl`,
      and `sl` is a plain Lock, not an RLock. The v323 note in the same function documents the
      same trap - it inlines its peer scan for exactly this reason.

      TEST: fly, exit to HQ, change aircraft, re-join with someone else in the arena. Expect a
      [TEARDOWN] line naming the re-join, and both pilots visible to each other afterwards.

