v337: [PLANES] byte-0 tab override (EXPERIMENTAL, now ON) + v336 nation-range fix.

      v336 FIRST: the catalog filter's `_have_side` was written `0 <= s.nation < 5` in v334,
      but NU/Neutral is camp 7. For an NU pilot that made _have_side False; with nothing
      staff-hidden for an admin, kept == ids, which fails the `len(kept) != len(ids)` guard, so
      NO filtered echo was sent and the client fell back to its own nation grouping. Range is
      now `< 8` (camps 5/6 unused, harmless to admit).

      v337: the 0x3a catalog echo controls only whether a plane is IN the hangar list - the
      client picks the nation TAB from the GAME_DEF plane-info array (byte 0). So PLANE_TEAMS
      camp 7 could keep the Me-163B out of other sides' lists but could not move it onto the NU
      tab. apply_plane_byte0_override() writes byte 0 directly; {118: 0x80} = bit 7 = camp 7.
      Placed AFTER apply_plane_teams (which rewrites byte 0 every run) and BEFORE both encoders
      - it was first written into the all-literals fallback, where the normal real-LZ path would
      have skipped it. Length-preserving, so pad alignment is untouched.
      GUARD: a value of 0x00 is REFUSED outright and logged, naming the v332 CTD. That value can
      never be written through this path again.
      RESULT: bit 7 is ACCEPTED - no CTD, unlike v332's 0x00. So the top bits of that byte are
      usable as camps, and it was specifically "no bits set" that the GAME_DEF parser rejected.
      PLANE_BYTE0_OVERRIDE_ENABLED shipped False and was turned on after a live test.

      *** KNOWN ISSUE - accepted for now, not fixed ***
