      on the JPN tab. So byte 0 moves a plane onto a tab, but the tab->slot mapping the client
      uses for DISPLAY is not the same indexing as PLANE_ROSTER slot order - the entry that
      appears on NU is some other airframe, and the JPN entry is not being vacated. Likely the
      same class of problem as the 2026-06-30 correction that rebuilt PLANE_ROSTER from the
      msg-58 catalog when it turned out the old list was in HANGAR DISPLAY order rather than
      slot order. Next step if this is picked up again: dump the client's msg-58 catalog while
      the override is active and compare display position against slot 118, rather than
