v332: [PLANES] STAFF-ONLY AIRFRAMES - the Me-163B is restricted to @HQ / @FA / @HOST pilots.
      It sits at PLANE_ROSTER slot 118 (0x76) and was showing up in the JAPANESE pool, which
      is both historically wrong and not wanted in normal play.
      TWO mechanisms are needed, and they do DIFFERENT jobs - doing only one is not enough:
        (1) GAME_DEF plane-block byte 0 -> 0x00. The gate is FA.exe FUN_00438330,
            flyable(plane,camp) = PLANE.field[0] & (1 << camp), and field[0] is record byte 0
            (stock 0x1f = bits 0..4 = all five camps). Zeroing it leaves no camp bit set, so
            the plane is flyable by NOBODY. Record length is unchanged, so no block growth, no
            MTU pressure, no 'max/used' line, and the LZ pad alignment is untouched.
            apply_plane_hide() runs AFTER apply_plane_teams() because that function rewrites
            byte 0 of every record and would otherwise undo the mask, and it runs
            unconditionally so the restriction holds even where per-team assignment is off.
        (2) The 0x3a catalog echo trim. PLANE_FILTER_VIA_CATALOG is True, which means
            apply_plane_teams deliberately leaves byte 0 at 0x1f and the real per-side filter
            lives in the 0x3a echo - and THAT is what builds the hangar list. So masking byte 0
            alone would leave the Komet visible-but-unselectable; trimming the catalog alone
            would hide it from the list while leaving it flyable by any path that bypasses the
            list. Both together hide it AND block it.
      Decided PER PLAYER at serve time: the GAME_DEF is rebuilt on every arena entry and on
      every on-demand 212, and both senders (send_arenalist_with_gamedefs,
      handle_gamedef_request) already have the session in scope, so hide_planes threads down
      through build_gamedef_212 -> build_lz_gamedef. No per-arena authoring, no client files,
      nothing to distribute - which is what the long-dormant "per-arena plane pool" TODO would
      otherwise have required.
      Tag test is a SUBSTRING match so '@FA' also admits '@FA3' and '@FAVG', and the tag may
      sit anywhere in the name ('Moira@HQ', 'Bopster@FA', '@HOST_Bob'). Verified that
      'HQ_Bob' and 'FAKE@HO' do NOT pass.
      Config: STAFF_ONLY_PLANES / STAFF_PLANE_TAGS. A name in STAFF_ONLY_PLANES that is not in
      PLANE_ROSTER is warned about at startup rather than silently ignored, and the active
      restriction is printed on boot.
      CAVEAT: a pilot RENAMED into a staff tag gains access on their next GAME_DEF serve, and
      one renamed out of it keeps access until then. Re-entering the arena refreshes it.

